<!-- An overview of this document -->
<section name="Overview" tag="overview">
Current usage of the Choices: structure is very disorganised, with each user
selecting their own particular way of storing options. Many fail to use the
<linkto url="http://www.thevillage.ndirect.co.uk/justin/info/choices.html">
correct</linkto> way of accessing the Choices: structure and some still
use files in their own directory structure.

<p>This suggests a central module to maintain configuration options for
applications. The files to be control will be textual, to prevent allow
user fixing of problems (if necessary).

<p>This module should provide :

<ul>
 <li>A means of reading options files (from Choices or an arbitrary location)
 <li>A means of writing options files (to the correct part of Choices or the
     original location
 <li>A means of collating related items within a file into 'groups'
</ul>

